{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken","id":921560,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Armored in Starlight : The Cage of the Penitent Eidolon Forsaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T10:51:15-07:00","id":921560,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Armored in Starlight : The Cage of the Penitent Eidolon Forsaken","content":"<b>The Cage of Penitent Eidolon Forsaken (Orihalcum and Starmetal Articulated Plate, Artifact ooooo)</b><br /> <br /> In the streets of Yu-Shan, rumor flies of a strange new menacing figure, lurking within the Crimson Panoply of Victory. They say he is clad in head to foot in heavy orihalcum articulated plate affixed with over a hundred delicate-looking prayer strips of starmetal with imperishable jade-paint, each written in Old Realm wards and scriptures against evil. Some say he is a new god, unknown to the greater community of divinities- a challenger to Ahlat with the support of the Shogun of the Crimson Banner. Others claim he is a spirit or automaton conjured by Sidereal magics, the first in an imperishable golden army with which to defend Heaven against Rakan Thulio.<br /> <br /> In truth, he is Penitent Eidolon Forsaken, a Solar of the Dawn Caste who Exalted while fighting alongside the Tepet legions against the Bull of the North. Horrified at having become the very monster what he sought to destroy, he fled the field, shortly thereafter turning himself in to an Immaculate temple- where he was intercepted by a Bronze Star of an unusually pragmatic bent, even for her faction.<br /> <br /> She smuggled the man, who now named himself as Penitent Eidolon Forsaken, into Yu-Shan. There, she saw to it that he would be confined in heavy chains of gold that could bind down his terrible divinity. Atop this, she affixed the hundred prayer strips, telling the Eidolon that they would channel his cursed power into something pure, giving his soul a chance at a more auspicious reincarnation. She then showed her work to Chejop Kejak; here was a Solar that would serve the Realm, a Lawgiver that would submit to proper authority. Kejak has been skeptical thus far- the plan reeks of risk -but even he cannot deny the effectiveness of the Penitent Eidolon Forsaken in handling tasks that would have risked Sidereal lives.<br /> <br /> The Cage of Penitent Eidolon Forsaken has three hearthstone slots, pressing into the gorget that encircles the wearer\u2019s neck.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Cage of Penitent Eidolon Forsaken</b><br /> <br /> Attuning to the Cage of Penitent Eidolon Forsaken costs a Solar, Sidereal or Getimian an additional six motes. However, so long as it is worn, the victim subsists without need for food or water, and is kept comfortable in any mundane weather. Moreover, the Cage conceals the nature of their divinity; their anima is transformed to pure white light, and their caste mark obscured behind the Old Realm glyph for \u2018Wicked\u2019.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>No Rest For the Forsaken</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent has no time to waste on such trivialities as rest if she is to redeem her forsaken soul. After using No Rest For the Forsaken, the bearer suffers no penalties for fatigue for the next day and night. Motes committed to this Charm remain committed until the bearer sleeps for at least eight hours.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Redeemed by Blasphemous Deeds</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent can find redemption in the destruction of beings even more blasphemous than herself; when she strike a blow which incapacitates or destroys an enemy demon or ghost, she may reflexively activate Redeemed by Blasphemous Deeds to gain 1 temporary point of Willpower, not to exceed her permanent Willpower.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unclean to Touch</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Counterattack<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent is too unclean to be touched, neither by a gentle caress nor a ruinous strike. When struck by a weapon at close range, she may use Unclean to Touch to attempt a reflexive Disarm gambit (Exalted p. 200) against her attacker as a counterattack, rolling her (Stamina + Resistance) for the attack. If she is struck by a barehanded attack, she may instead make a reflexive Withering counterattack against her attacker, again using her (Stamina + Resistance) and using her (Soak) as the base damage of the attack, Unclean to Touch cannot be used in response to another counterattack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Too Wretched For Death</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m / 1 Hardness; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent cannot die until they have atoned for the sin of what they have become; alas that atonement will always be beyond their reach. Once per scene, she may reflexive increase her Hardness against a single decisive attack, at a cost of 2 motes per point of hardness.<br /> Too Wretched For Death is reset when the wearer has no remaining -0, -1 or -2 health levels.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Deceived No Longer</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m or 4m / Willpower; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> No Rest For the Forsaken, Redeemed by Blasphemous Deeds, Unclean to Touch, Too Wretched For Death<br /> <br /> The penitent realizes the truth of her Exalted station, and casts away the illusions that would chain and deceive her. She may spend 6 motes to reflexively pay the Willpower cost for resisting any social influence or other mind altering effects; the cost is reduced to 4 motes when resisting effects with the Psyche keyword.<br /> <br /> Additionally, upon learning Deceived No Longer, the bearer no longer needs to commit an additional 6 motes to attune to the Cage, and the glyph for \u2018Wicked\u2019 which obscures her caste mark is replaced with the glyph for \u2018Righteous\u2019.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T16:21:47-07:00","id":921739,"title":"","content":"This makes me wary.<br /> <br /> The way it's presented reminds me a lot of the stuff in TAW where it stopped making the things it was theoretically supposed to show as heroes and saviors as kind of assholes. Some of the effects are a bit iffy (The Hardness Power and the 3m Disarm Gambit are both really incredibly good), and the actual backstory is kind of gruesome to little benefit.<br /> <br /> Is this character a PC? He doesn't feel like it; it seems like he's an NPC used to show how Sidereals (or at least Bronze Factions) are uncaring and brutal, but if he's an NPC then I don't think he needs his one of a kind specific artifact armor to be stated out like this either. It doesn't feel like a 5 dot artifact despite it's powerful charms, either, because it doesn't really offer a new, unique series of effects; it's just a bunch of kind of one off powers that don't have much connection to each other.<br /> <br /> I also don't understand what the last power even does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:17:02-07:00","id":921762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921739#post921739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me wary.<br /> <br /> The way it's presented reminds me a lot of the stuff in TAW where it stopped making the things it was theoretically supposed to show as heroes and saviors as kind of assholes. Some of the effects are a bit iffy (The Hardness Power and the 3m Disarm Gambit are both really incredibly good), and the actual backstory is kind of gruesome to little benefit.<br /> <br /> Is this character a PC? He doesn't feel like it; it seems like he's an NPC used to show how Sidereals (or at least Bronze Factions) are uncaring and brutal, but if he's an NPC then I don't think he needs his one of a kind specific artifact armor to be stated out like this either. It doesn't feel like a 5 dot artifact despite it's powerful charms, either, because it doesn't really offer a new, unique series of effects; it's just a bunch of kind of one off powers that don't have much connection to each other.<br /> <br /> I also don't understand what the last power even does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, powers first-<br /> <br /> Unclean to Touch is modeled straight on Solar Counterattack- same cost, more restricted effect but with a different attribute/ability combination.<br /> <br /> Too Wretched for Death *is* very mean. With a base Hardness of 10 for being Heavy Artifact Armor, it's pretty likely to no-sell at least one attack relatively cheap, and then a second attack (at probably far greater cost) late in the fight. OTOH, at 2m per die, it gets expensive in a big damn hurry, and is basically useless if it can't completely no sell an attack- compare to Adamant Skin Technique. Coupled with the limited use, and it seemed like a good backup to other Resistance based fighting powers.<br /> <br /> Deceived No Longer is, on review of Integrity, probably too strong. The idea was essentially that it was the apothesis charm- at this point, the bearer of the Cage is no longer in the thrall of the Sidereals (or anyone else)- they can use Essence to shake off social influence, and resist Pysche effects more easily than natural influence. So, for instance, a Solar targetted by Hypnotic Tongue Technique could burn 12m on Deceived No Longer to resist a successfully given command- 4m per Willpower. Compared to Transcendent Hero's Meditation, that's probably too good. Meanwhile, the non-magical influence resistance was being built from Spirit-Tempering Practice- more expensive, more limited (only letting you resist influence, not general purpose willpower), but without the once per scene limitation. It needs some tweaking.<br /> <br /> Re: Rating<br /> <br /> That's a fair cop. The Cage really could be an Artifact 4. It was kind of bigger in my head. I mean, it's not Volcano Cutter, but I think it's on par with Black Wind for narrative and magical power,<br /> <br /> Re: The purpose and the character<br /> <br /> Penitent Eidolon Forsaken was, in fact, an NPC from the last game I was playing in- a *thing* that was terrifyingly strong and working with the Wyld Hunt that was chasing us. I got the rough story from the ST as to the nature of the Eidolon afterwards. There, the Cage was pure Starmetal, which he (as a Solar) was paying double attunement cost for, as a means of 'locking down his evil power'- and also because Starmetal Articulated Plate was fucking *hax* and meant there was very little we could do to hurt that sumbitch.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Bronze Faction going 'There's too many Solars to just murderface right now, and too many other, very dire threats. Can we solve one problem with another?' - but not trusting the Solars further than they can throw them, and so trying to condition a self-loathing member of the Dynasty that happened to Exalted as a Solar to their purposes. Deceived No Longer also kind of points to the probable outcome of *that* plot arc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 06-26-2016, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:37:23-07:00","id":921774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921762#post921762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, powers first-<br /> <br /> Unclean to Touch is modeled straight on Solar Counterattack- same cost, more restricted effect but with a different attribute/ability combination.<br /> <br /> Too Wretched for Death *is* very mean. With a base Hardness of 10 for being Heavy Artifact Armor, it's pretty likely to no-sell at least one attack relatively cheap, and then a second attack (at probably far greater cost) late in the fight. OTOH, at 2m per die, it gets expensive in a big damn hurry, and is basically useless if it can't completely no sell an attack- compare to Adamant Skin Technique. Coupled with the limited use, and it seemed like a good backup to other Resistance based fighting powers.<br /> <br /> Deceived No Longer is, on review of Integrity, probably too strong. The idea was essentially that it was the apothesis charm- at this point, the bearer of the Cage is no longer in the thrall of the Sidereals (or anyone else)- they can use Essence to shake off social influence, and resist Pysche effects more easily than natural influence. So, for instance, a Solar targetted by Hypnotic Tongue Technique could burn 12m on Deceived No Longer to resist a successfully given command- 4m per Willpower. Compared to Transcendent Hero's Meditation, that's probably too good. Meanwhile, the non-magical influence resistance was being built from Spirit-Tempering Practice- more expensive, more limited (only letting you resist influence, not general purpose willpower), but without the once per scene limitation. It needs some tweaking.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unclean to Touch is better then Solar Counterattack.<br /> <br /> Solar Counterattack is a Decisive-Only attack; while it does give an attack that actually does damage, it can only do it once. Unclean To Touch is the same mote cost, but can be used against anything and doesn't drain your Initiative; it's only a small mote drain and is spammable because it's effect isn't damage. Especially if you're supposed to give the counterattack an Accuracy (the equivalent of a Light weapon, I guess); then this charm has a much higher dice pool as well. There's no reason to not use it on every attack that hits you because it's cheap and brutally effective, especially given the huge amount of Soak you can get (against unarmed) and how strong disarm could be (against Melee people). At base level you're looking at a 3m counterattack that can be either Withering or Decisive, giving it wide chances, and if it's a Melee attack it's literally just Solar Counter Attack, but better because using it once doesn't restrict you to a 3 dice counter attack, instead you just respond with your massive Soak (Artifact Heavy Armor means your base damage on a Withering Melee Counterattack is amazing.<br /> <br /> To space this out with some math here;<br /> <br /> You're asking for a Withering Counter Attack using Soak as Base Damage. Assuming you're adding the Light Weapon statistics to it (Since it seems to be a Brawl attack), just for Accuracy- because you aren't clear if you do or not-, this withering counterattack has the best statline in the game, arguably. It starts at Accuracy 5, Damage 11 if you have 0 Soak, which is impossible. This character also seems built to be a super resistance one, or rather the armor seems to work best with someone whose already heavily invested in Stamina and Resistance, so I'd say the likely amount of Stamina is between 3 and 5. The statlines for these attacks are as followed, starting at 3 and going to 5.<br /> <br /> Accuracy 5, Damage 14<br /> Accuracy 5, Damage 15<br /> Accuracy 5, Damage 16.<br /> <br /> So even at only Stamina 3, you already have a weapon that is as reliable as a Light Weapon but as damaging as a Heavy Weapon. This character may also constantly use this highly damaging, highly accurate counter attack, since it's Dual, that means that's the withering Version. He may use it Decisively- where against a Melee target it's 'just' an Initiative free Disarm that can still be spammed because it will only subtract the gambit's successes, while against a Brawler it's just straight up Solar Counterattack-, or Witheringly, which already makes it more flexible then Solar Counterattack, and allows either- again- more Disarming with a highly flexible weapon that has high accuracy, avoiding the issue of Gambits having Decisive accuracy-, or if it's a brawler, having the best accuracy and damage that the game allows on a weapon without specific evocations to increase it's base levels.<br /> <br /> It's not actually 'more restricted'; it's more restricted in the part where Solar Counterattack can do anything at all, but it also has a secondary function that Solar Counterattack can not do at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:41:14-07:00","id":921775,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the solution might just be to limit Unclean to Touch to the reflexive Disarm and have it cost Initiative like a normal gambit does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:12:21-07:00","id":921785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921774#post921774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unclean to Touch is better then Solar Counterattack.<br /> <br /> Solar Counterattack is a Decisive-Only attack; while it does give an attack that actually does damage, it can only do it once. Unclean To Touch is the same mote cost, but can be used against anything and doesn't drain your Initiative;</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. It provides a reflexive decisive gambit. If the attack misses, you lose intiative as per a failed decisive attack; if you succeed, it costs initative equal to the difficulty of the gambit (Exalted p. 199); why did you assume that it cost no initative?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921774#post921774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's only a small mote drain and is spammable because it's effect isn't damage. Especially if you're supposed to give the counterattack an Accuracy (the equivalent of a Light weapon, I guess);</div> </div> </div> </div>Again- why are you assuming the armor provides accuracy at all when such is not specified, let alone the *literal* best accuracy possible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921774#post921774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then this charm has a much higher dice pool as well. There's no reason to not use it on every attack that hits you because it's cheap and brutally effective, especially given the huge amount of Soak you can get (against unarmed) and how strong disarm could be (against Melee people). At base level you're looking at a 3m counterattack that can be either Withering or Decisive, giving it wide chances, and if it's a Melee attack it's literally just Solar Counter Attack, but better because using it once doesn't restrict you to a 3 dice counter attack, instead you just respond with your massive Soak (Artifact Heavy Armor means your base damage on a Withering Melee Counterattack is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible the withering counterattack needs to be toned down. In a one on one fight, it's pretty brutal against an unarmed fighter. Of course, an unarmed fighter going against someone in heavy artifact armor is already going to be in a world of pain, so it's a question of degrees.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt seems like you're basically making every assumption possible towards 'This power is crazy broken' - now, that indincates it needs clarification, but I geniuenly don't understand how you came to the conclusions you did, or how to provide clarification short of restating the base rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T19:13:29-07:00","id":921811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921785#post921785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect. It provides a reflexive decisive gambit. If the attack misses, you lose intiative as per a failed decisive attack; if you succeed, it costs initative equal to the difficulty of the gambit (Exalted p. 199); why did you assume that it cost no initative?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again- why are you assuming the armor provides accuracy at all when such is not specified, let alone the *literal* best accuracy possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's possible the withering counterattack needs to be toned down. In a one on one fight, it's pretty brutal against an unarmed fighter. Of course, an unarmed fighter going against someone in heavy artifact armor is already going to be in a world of pain, so it's a question of degrees.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt seems like you're basically making every assumption possible towards 'This power is crazy broken' - now, that indincates it needs clarification, but I geniuenly don't understand how you came to the conclusions you did, or how to provide clarification short of restating the base rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>You understand that all withering attacks add an accuracy as a baseline rule right? If this withering attack specifically does not add an accuracy, you should clarify this. I instead based it off of the idea of it being an unarmed attack, which would use the Light weapon stats as listed in the book.If your evocation is unclear enough that it can be read in such a way, you should clarify the language. If you're using new or specific interactions that in all other cases do not exist, you should clarify them. There are no such things as withering attacks that do not add an accuracy as a baseline; if they exist they would be within the zones of charms, and they would call it out. As a note, even if it 'just' used the Heavy Weapon accuracy, it would still be flatly superior to an artifact Heavy Weapon as it would do more base damage.<br /> <br /> You should at least understand that a 3 mote charm at Essence 2 that makes you effectively invulnerable or unstoppable to an entire combat ability is iffy at best.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you are saying that losing between 2-4 Initiative, regardless of hit or miss, is equivalent to Solar Counterattack completely resetting you. if you miss with Solar Counterattack, you lose the same Initiative at the same level. While if you hit, you arguably can't use Solar Counter Attack again because you will have 3 (Or slightly more) Initiative, which makes it difficult to break Hardness against an opponent with Artifact armor- requiring you to use even more motes-, while this one simply has his gambit roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 06-26-2016, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T06:44:51-07:00","id":921974,"title":"","content":"Hm. Alright, I'm convinced.<br /> <br /> How about the following?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unclean to Touch</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent is too unclean to be touched, neither by a gentle caress nor a ruinous strike. When struck at close range, she may use Unclean to Touch to scorch her opponent; she rolls 1 + (anima rank) dice, inflicting that many points of initative damage. Initative damage dealt in this fashion is not gained by the bearer, but she does gain the initiative crash bonus if this results in the attacker crashing. When struck by an opponent in initative crash, Unclean to Touch instead inflicts 1 + (anima rank) dice of lethal damage. In both cases, this damage is reduced by Hardness, and may be reduced to zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:22:23-07:00","id":922073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921974#post921974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Alright, I'm convinced.<br /> <br /> How about the following?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unclean to Touch</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent is too unclean to be touched, neither by a gentle caress nor a ruinous strike. When struck at close range, she may use Unclean to Touch to scorch her opponent; she rolls 1 + (anima rank) dice, inflicting that many points of initative damage. Initative damage dealt in this fashion is not gained by the bearer, but she does gain the initiative crash bonus if this results in the attacker crashing. When struck by an opponent in initative crash, Unclean to Touch instead inflicts 1 + (anima rank) dice of lethal damage. In both cases, this damage is reduced by Hardness, and may be reduced to zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>This charm is much better. It's an interesting idea to reduce by hardness instead of soak but you have called it out so linguistics-wise it's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:31:18-07:00","id":922075,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:32:58-07:00","id":922076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=921974#post921974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Alright, I'm convinced.<br /> <br /> How about the following?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unclean to Touch</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The penitent is too unclean to be touched, neither by a gentle caress nor a ruinous strike. When struck at close range, she may use Unclean to Touch to scorch her opponent; she rolls 1 + (anima rank) dice, inflicting that many points of initative damage. Initative damage dealt in this fashion is not gained by the bearer, but she does gain the initiative crash bonus if this results in the attacker crashing. When struck by an opponent in initative crash, Unclean to Touch instead inflicts 1 + (anima rank) dice of lethal damage. In both cases, this damage is reduced by Hardness, and may be reduced to zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't this have the Counterattack keyword? It seems to function as one. Should note when in the attack this functions (after hitting, before damage, after damage, is damage still rolled after the attack, even if they are killed by this?) for clarity. Also Hardness is equal to 0 when a foe is in Initiative Crash, so does this evocation allow Hardness in Crash in the foe?<br /> <br /> Other than these clarifications, I functionally like this one a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:31:18-07:00","id":922114,"title":"","content":"Re: Counterattack<br /> <br /> Hm. I'm not sure; it doesn't involve an attack roll- it's just a thing that happens. Is getting burned by a hot stove a counterattack of the stove?<br /> <br /> Re: Hardness in Crash<br /> <br /> Newp. If you're in crash, attacking the dude in the Cage is a poor choice of things to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:46:46-07:00","id":922126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=922114#post922114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Counterattack<br /> <br /> Hm. I'm not sure; it doesn't involve an attack roll- it's just a thing that happens. Is getting burned by a hot stove a counterattack of the stove?<br /> <br /> Re: Hardness in Crash<br /> <br /> Newp. If you're in crash, attacking the dude in the Cage is a poor choice of things to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant that you specified that damage is reduced by Hardness, but since the Lethal damage can only occur when they are Crashed and Hardness is 0 when Crashed, it just seems like that would never come up.<br /> <br /> I see your point about Counterattack, but it's at least important to consider the situation where Person A attacks Person B (where B wears the Cage). B burns A in the process of the attack, and the damage is sufficient to kill A. Did A's attack complete? Did B still get damaged by it? When does that occur in the process? Any place is probably fine, but it's important to specify what happens there. As far as the Counterattack keyword itself, if you don't use it, then person A can counterattack the burning power themselves and that might be nastier than whatever the Cage pumps out. So person A gets 2 (potentially bigger) attacks on B, due to this incoming damage. Counterattack keyword would keep A from using counterattacks against B.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts, take it or leave it. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:51:04-07:00","id":922132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=922126#post922126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just meant that you specified that damage is reduced by Hardness, but since the Lethal damage can only occur when they are Crashed and Hardness is 0 when Crashed, it just seems like that would never come up.<br /> <br /> I see your point about Counterattack, but it's at least important to consider the situation where Person A attacks Person B (where B wears the Cage). B burns A in the process of the attack, and the damage is sufficient to kill A. Did A's attack complete? Did B still get damaged by it? When does that occur in the process? Any place is probably fine, but it's important to specify what happens there. As far as the Counterattack keyword itself, if you don't use it, then person A can counterattack the burning power themselves and that might be nastier than whatever the Cage pumps out. So person A gets 2 (potentially bigger) attacks on B, due to this incoming damage. Counterattack keyword would keep A from using counterattacks against B.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts, take it or leave it. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Crash<br /> <br /> Hm, good point. *thinks* I think I'll just model it after the Dragonblooded anima description, and have any amount of Hardness block the damage. Actually, might just have it fix at 3d as well; the anima bit is flavorful but adds complexity for a minimum of value.<br /> <br /> Re: Counterattack<br /> <br /> Ah, I see what you're saying. The burn should happen in response to a successful attack- that way, the success / failure of the attack has already been determined.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T12:13:10-07:00","id":922146,"title":"","content":"Attunement bonus: Wow this is a pretty big bonus. Going without food/water/waste and disguising the anima is incredibly potent. I'd probably say only one or the other, as this attunement effect is really strong, then again I'm lazy when it comes to attunement effects so<br /> <br /> No Rest For the Forsaken: Needs Stackable Keyword.<br /> <br /> Redeemed by Blasphemous Deeds: Fine<br /> <br /> Unclean to Touch: It was taken care of by flare, so fine.<br /> <br /> Too Wretched For Death: What is the limit of this hardness specifically?<br /> <br /> Deceived No Longer: So you're kinda replicating a Solar charm and dropping attunement?<br /> <br /> This armour feels like an artifact 4 rather than a 5. We don't have a lot of 5's go along as baseline, but Dauntless itself appears to grant more impressive powers than this. Its fine don't get me wrong, but I feel its more at home as an artifact 4 armour. An artifact 5 armour should at least have an effect that makes you scream &quot;GO AHEAD FOOLS! BREAK YOUR WEAPONS UPON MY ARMOUR!&quot; somewhere in there if Volcano Cutter is any indication in terms of power escalation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:23:33-07:00","id":922308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=922146#post922146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attunement bonus: Wow this is a pretty big bonus. Going without food/water/waste and disguising the anima is incredibly potent. I'd probably say only one or the other, as this attunement effect is really strong, then again I'm lazy when it comes to attunement effects so<br /> <br /> No Rest For the Forsaken: Needs Stackable Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh. Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=922146#post922146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too Wretched For Death: What is the limit of this hardness specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is none. OTOH it'll get expensive in a hurry. I expect it'll no-sell the first attack relatively cheap, and then you get one more after the reset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=922146#post922146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deceived No Longer: So you're kinda replicating a Solar charm and dropping attunement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically. Although I'd forgotten that Spirit Maintaining Manuver was a thing &gt;&lt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/921560-sidereals-wfhl-armored-in-starlight-the-cage-of-the-penitent-eidolon-forsaken?p=922146#post922146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This armour feels like an artifact 4 rather than a 5. We don't have a lot of 5's go along as baseline, but Dauntless itself appears to grant more impressive powers than this. Its fine don't get me wrong, but I feel its more at home as an artifact 4 armour. An artifact 5 armour should at least have an effect that makes you scream &quot;GO AHEAD FOOLS! BREAK YOUR WEAPONS UPON MY ARMOUR!&quot; somewhere in there if Volcano Cutter is any indication in terms of power escalation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean- I feel that. I said upthread that the Cage could easily have been an Artifact 4- but I wanted to push it up some. Frankly, Dauntless I would consider over-costed at Artifact 5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}